WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.963
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module.

2
00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:05.745
You'll say what DDoS
infrastructure protection,

3
00:00:05.745 --> 00:00:10.475
I P Protection and Network Protection each
give, and what neither paid tier covers.

4
00:00:10.475 --> 00:00:15.037
You'll check that every public I P
is protected, logged and alerting.

5
00:00:15.037 --> 00:00:19.323
You'll explain why a simulation runs
only through an approved partner,

6
00:00:19.323 --> 00:00:21.762
and only against your own protected I Ps.

7
00:00:21.762 --> 00:00:26.280
You'll take a web application firewall
policy from detection to prevention,

8
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:30.225
with request body inspection, the
current rule set and a rate limit.

9
00:00:30.225 --> 00:00:32.497
And you'll prove it blocks a test request,

10
00:00:32.497 --> 00:00:35.250
and roll it back if it
blocks legitimate traffic.

11
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.681
You need Module 1 and its public I P
query, and the guide's decision record

12
00:00:39.681 --> 00:00:44.330
template, because the DDoS tier and
the Front Door tier are recorded there.
